From 57a85c7e374b0f8ea40456c5b782a51304cb7093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio Campolim <250239356+fabiocampolim-design@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:45:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 0/3] MUMPS thread safety, plus two documentation clarifications

Hello,

while building a teaching notebook against Kwant 1.5 I ran into a crash
that is not documented anywhere I could find: calling kwant.smatrix from
several threads at once segfaults the interpreter whenever the MUMPS
solver is in use, because MUMPS is not re-entrant.  Patch 1 serializes
the calls into MUMPS behind one lock (the linear solves then run one at a
time, which is the only correct behaviour available without an MPI
build), adds a threaded-vs-serial test that skips when MUMPS is absent,
documents the constraint on the solver's reference page and adds a
whatsnew entry.  I validated the change by loading the patched module
into an installed 1.5.0 (python-mumps 0.0.6, numpy 2.5.1, Python 3.13,
Windows): 3/3 threaded sweeps identical to the serial result, while the
unpatched module crashes every time.  A minimal reproducer is in the
commit message.

Patches 2 and 3 are documentation only: the FAQ example for coloring
sublattices silently breaks on a finalized system (site_color is passed
the site index there, not a Site), and the wraparound docstring never
says what k_x, k_y, ... are or that they are 2*pi-periodic, which bit me
when computing a Berry curvature density on a non-rectangular lattice.

Unrelated but worth a maintainer's attention: with numpy >= 2.5 the
released 1.5.0 fails in kwant.physics.magnetic_gauge for every 2-D
system (np.cross on 2-vectors was removed in numpy 2.5.0); the fix has
been on main since January 2025 but there is no release carrying it, and
the 1.5.0 packages do not pin numpy.  I will open an issue with the
details; a 1.5.1 or a conda-forge repodata patch would fix it for users.

Based on main at ef12fa0.  Happy to rework anything.

[name]

[name] (3):
  solvers.mumps: serialize calls into MUMPS, which is not re-entrant
  doc: FAQ: explain what a site_color function receives for a finalized
    system
  wraparound: document the meaning and periodicity of the momentum
    parameters

